				<desc>apply rotor brake</desc>
			</key>
			
			<key>
				<name>q a z d</name>
				<desc>Pan the search light arround. Only available in specific configurations.</desc>
			</key>
			
			
			<key>
				<name>MMB</name>
				<desc>adjust power lever (middle mouse button)</desc>
			</key>
			
		
			
		<line> Rotorbrake can only be activated from the lever on the overhead panel</line>
		<line>If you are using HDR, then you need to enable the specific HDR panel lights from the EC120 Menu.</line>
 <line>Using the HDR panel lights while not in HDR will produce very strange results.</line>	
		<line> </line>
		<line> EC-120B+ Manual start proceedure.</line>
		<line>PREPARATION</line>
		<line> Rotorbrake...forward / released  ( overhead )</line>
		<line> Fuel shut-off lever ... forward and secured ( overhead ) </line>
		<line>Battery..ON  ( Main switch panel )</line>
		<line>Gen...  OFF ( Main switch panel )</line>
		<line>Instrument light ...as required ( Default OFF. Main switch panel )</line>
		<line>PITOT as required ( Main switch panel )</line>
		<line> Nav lights and beacons as required ( Main switch panel )</line>
		<line> Fuel pump ON ( Main switch panel ).</line>
		<line>Twist grip...Idle position ( power to 63% using Middle mouse button - hold and scroll mouse up to increase.) </line>
		<line> </line>
		<line>ENGINE START</line>
		<line>CPW... check GOV light is OFF </line>
		<line>Fuel pump.... ON (FUEL P light should be ON. Run for 30 sec before starting ! )</line>
		<line>GENE ... OFF ( GENE warning light should be off )</line>
		<line>Starter Selector... ON ( Orange long button on the site of the collective. Click to engage )</line>
		<line>Check parameters : Ng... increase   TOT ...below limits   Engine oil pressure ....checked </line>
		<line>N1 = 20% disengage starter. ( Orange long button on the site of the collective. Click again to disengage )</line>
		<line>When N1 > 63% you are art idle</line>
		<line>When N1= 63%, GENE- ON, BATTERY-OFF</line>
		<line>Fuel Pump ... OFF </line>
		<line>Warning lights... all out, exc.GENE</line>
		<line> Twist grip.... flight position ( power to 97%)</line>
		<line></line>
		<line>FIRST FLIGHT</line>
		<line>Once you are fueled up and powered up, takeoff is fairly neutral while in standard trim.</line>
		<line>Takeoff requires slight right pedal and Cyclic slightly in the 4 o'clock position.</line>
		<line></line>
		<line>Emergancy Floatation system:-</line>
			<line>The floats are available  through the EQUIPMENT-FUEL + PAYLOAD menu.</line>
			<line>Once fitted the arming and trigger systems become available in the cockpit.</line>
			<line>On the Main Switch panel, the FLOATS button, will light up green when pressed when the system is armed</line>
			<line>On the right side of the main panel, the red Trigger toggle will become available.</line>
			<line>Once the system is armed, clicking the trigger will infate the floats.</line>
			<line> Clicking the trigger again while on dry land will repack the floats and re set the system</line>
			<line></line>
			<line></line>
			<line> SAR Menu option - THIS IS JUST A FUN   MULTIPLAYER FEATURE !!</line>
			<line> If you crash your Cougar, you can use this menu option to call on another EC120 </line>
			<line>or any other chopper running the script, to retrieve your broken chopper and you, as an underslung load.</line>
			<line> </line>
<line>AUTOPILOT V3 </line>
<line>The Autopilot is now able to control  speed, altitude and heading. Autopilot is only usable  between 30-140kts</line>
<line>Heading modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>Speed modes can be used without any other Autopilot function being active.</line>
<line>****  Altitude modes can only be used in conjunction with speed mode being being active. This includes the use of Vertical Speed mode.  ***</line>
<line>AUTOPILOT ISSUES !!!!!</line>
<line>When disengaging the AP entirely or from a singe mode, the  control inputs will snap to your actual cyclic/colective/pedal positions as soon as you  move any of them.</line>
<line>This is unavoidable as  the sim can not physically move your cyclic/colective/pedal positions to match the Autopilots input.</line>
<line>The best advice to minimise the sudden change of input would be for you to  have your cyclic/colective/pedal positions ready in approximatly correct positions  to minimise the "snap".</line>

		</help>
